  "title": "A collar is a bullish call spread in disguise",
  "summary": "A collar is long stock, a long put just below the price and a short call above it. By put-call parity, stock plus a long put is a synthetic long call. Add the short call and you have a debit call spread at the same strikes. The speaker models both on Microsoft: the expiry payoffs have the same shape.",
